course: dictionary
lesson: 11350
title: Zing: a word with energy
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Zing is an informal word with more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which meaning is right. It can mean energy and excitement, as in «adding some zing» to a story. It can also mean a sharp, fresh taste, like lemon or ginger.
explain: Zing can also be a sound. A zing is a high, ringing or whistling noise, like something flying fast past your ear. The verb zing means to move very fast with that high sound. In a story, zing often shows speed, as with an arrow.
explain: The example sentences use zing for a sudden, sharp feeling. «Bumping it sends a zinging feeling down the arm» describes a quick jolt of tingling, not a taste or a sound. Ask yourself what fits the sentence, then check your meaning by putting it in place of the word.
fact: Zing is an informal word for energy, excitement or liveliness.
fact: Zing can also mean a sharp, fresh, tangy taste, like lemon or ginger.
fact: A zing is a high, ringing or whistling sound, like something flying fast.
fact: To zing means to move very fast with a high sound.
fact: In writing, adding zing means making something more lively and interesting.
exercise: «The lemon added a zing to the cake.» What does zing mean here? | A feeling of sadness | *A sharp, fresh, tangy taste | A long, slow walk | A heavy, dull sound
exercise: Mia says her story needs some zing. What does she want? | A quieter, sadder ending | A map of the town | *More energy and excitement | Fewer words on every page
exercise: «The arrow gave a zing as it flew past.» What does zing describe? | *A high whistling sound of something moving fast | A bright colour on the wall | A question from the teacher | A type of cold drink
test: «The new song had so much zing that everyone started dancing.» Which meaning fits best? | A ringing bell in the hall | A cold winter morning | Feeling very tired and sleepy | *Energy and excitement
test: In US slang, what does it mean to zing someone? | *To make a cheeky joke at them | To give them a big hug | To count them one by one | To sing very quietly to them
exam: Jayden says zing always means a taste. Which answer is correct? | Zing means very old | Zing is the name of a colour | *Not always: zing can also mean energy, a high sound, moving fast or a cheeky joke | Yes, zing only ever means a taste
